target: workflows/refine
version: 1
validations:
  - name: refine-modules-exist
    type: file_exists
    severity: error
    args:
      paths:
        - "intentc/refine/__init__.py"
        - "intentc/refine/workflow.py"
        - "intentc/refine/tests/test_*.py"
        - "intentc/build/agents/prompts/refine.prompt"
        - "intentc/build/agents/prompts/refine_bake.prompt"

  - name: refine-prompts-match-artifacts
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "cmp {intent_dir}/workflows/refine/prompts/refine.prompt {output_dir}/intentc/build/agents/prompts/refine.prompt && cmp {intent_dir}/workflows/refine/prompts/refine_bake.prompt {output_dir}/intentc/build/agents/prompts/refine_bake.prompt"

  - name: refine-tests-pass
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "uv run pytest {output_dir}/intentc/refine {output_dir}/intentc/build {output_dir}/intentc/cli -q"

  - name: refine-help-runs
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "uv run intentc refine --help"
      expect_output: "--bake"

  - name: refine-unknown-target-is-usage-error
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "uv run intentc refine does/not/exist; test $? -eq 2"
      expect_output: "Unknown feature"

  - name: refine-unbuilt-target-is-usage-error
    type: command_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      cwd: "."
      command: "uv run intentc refine workflows/refine -o never_built_output_dir; test $? -eq 2"
      expect_output: "has not been built"

  - name: refine-session-lifecycle
    type: agent_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      rubric: |
        Verify the refine workflow tests (MockAgent, MockVersionControl, real
        SQLiteBackend, temporary directories, no claude binary) demonstrate:
        (1) starting a session on an output directory with uncommitted changes, or on
        a target that is pending/failed, is refused before any agent is created;
        (2) a session persists a RefinementSession row with status "recording", the
        base commit, and the journal text the mock agent wrote to journal_path;
        (3) resuming appends to the same journal and passes the prior journal text in
        RefineContext.journal; (4) a session's RefineContext carries the target's
        artifacts and the agent's write paths cover only the output directory and
        the session directory; (5) abandon restores base_commit in the output
        directory and marks the session "abandoned"; (6) intentc build refuses with
        exit 2 while a session is open for a target in its build set.

  - name: refine-bake-loop
    type: agent_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      rubric: |
        Verify tests show the bake: snapshots the refined tree via
        version_control.snapshot without moving HEAD; calls agent.refine_bake once
        with a RefineContext whose diff, files_by_owner, journal and snapshot_dir are
        populated; then commits the target's feature directory as a dedicated
        intent commit (message "refine <target>: attempt <n> [session:<id8>]", only
        when it changed), runs builder.clean, builder.build for the target WITHOUT
        force (the BuildOptions passed to the builder must have force false, so
        already-built ancestors are not regenerated), and run_differencing, in that
        order; a "divergent" DifferencingResponse causes a second refine_bake call
        whose previous_errors contain the failing dimension's name and rationale; a
        rebuild whose validate step fails feeds one "<name>: <reason>" entry per
        failed validation (read back from storage) plus the failing step's summary,
        where a failed step is one with status "failure"; after profile.retries
        attempts the snapshot is restored into the output directory, the target
        status is "outdated", the session is "failed" and the .ic/.icv edits remain;
        --bake on a target whose latest session is "failed" re-bakes it reusing the
        stored snapshot_id without calling version_control.snapshot again; on success
        the session is "baked" with bake_generation_id set and the journal file
        deleted; with --no-compare run_differencing is never called; an AgentError
        raised by run_differencing is retried up to profile.retries calls and then
        fails the attempt with a "compare: agent error" entry, without the whole
        bake crashing; an unexpected exception inside an attempt leaves the session
        "failed" (not "baking") before propagating, and the CLI prints "Agent error:"
        with exit 1 rather than a traceback for an AgentError. Verify log lines use
        the prefix "bake n/N:" (no square brackets) and that render_refine_summary
        escapes markup so a generalisation containing "[x]" is printed verbatim. Verify that refine_bake with
        a missing response file raises AgentError rather than synthesising a
        response.

  - name: refine-prompts-encode-the-contract
    type: agent_validation
    severity: error
    args:
      rubric: |
        Read the bundled refine.prompt and refine_bake.prompt. Verify refine.prompt
        tells the agent to append a journal entry per ask with Asked / Decided /
        Rule / Changed / Check fields, forbids editing anything under intent/, and
        renders {journal}, {journal_path}, {artifacts} and {seed_prompt}. Verify
        refine_bake.prompt instructs the agent to fold rules into the existing
        intent structure rather than appending a refinements section, to turn every
        Check into a deterministic validation where possible, never to weaken
        existing requirements unless the journal reverses them, to save pasted
        schemas/mocks as declared artifacts, to restrict edits to the target's .ic,
        .icv and feature directory, and to write a RefineBakeResponse JSON with
        status, summary, files_modified, artifacts_added, generalizations and
        open_questions to {response_file}.
